From 450dce9ec0b71961fae56dad9e0014e6bfbe023b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 12:08:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02821/11362] [outer-loop] Kaggle build kernel: BUILD-ONLY +
 diagnostics (fix the 20GB-disk v4 failure)

Diagnosed the v4 ERROR: the kernel downloaded the 5.9GB GGUF AND built 4 CUDA archs into the ~20GB
/kaggle/working -> disk exhaustion. Rewrote the kernel build-only: NO GGUF download (the GGUF + smoke
are separate, disk-controlled concerns), -j2 (nvcc is memory-heavy; avoid an OOM-kill), and full
df/free + tee'd build.log + build_report.json captured to the output so any re-failure is recoverable
via `kaggle kernels output` (the v4 error was only in the web log). Builds ON Kaggle to match CUDA
12.8/driver exactly (local CUDA 13.3 + missing sm_60 make a local build risky). Output = the
binary+libs Dataset that the submission points CARNOT_LLAMA_SERVER at.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
